      "instance_name": "crack_addict_stereotype",
      "label": "Crack Addict Stereotype",
      "description": "A harmful and inaccurate stereotype that associates individuals with a 'crack addict' appearance with criminality, moral decay, and social marginalization. This stereotype is rooted in racist and classist assumptions and has been used to dehumanize and stigmatize people who use drugs, particularly in impoverished communities, often conflating appearance with inherent character flaws.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
